 Alternatively, note that in the standard KMP LPS construction, we do:
   while j > 0 and s[i] != s[j]:
        j = lps[j-1]

 Because the LPS array at index j-1 gives the length of the longest proper prefix that is also a suffix for the substring ending at j-1.

 Let me explain:

 The LPS array (lps[i]) for i from 0 to n-1, where lps[i] is the length of the longest proper prefix of the substring s[0:i] that is also a suffix of that substring.

