        j = lps[i-1]   # but note: in our code, j is maintained from the previous iteration.

 However, our code uses a different approach: we maintain j from the previous step and do not reset j to lps[i-1] at the start of the loop. 

 Actually, the standard way is:

   i = 1
   j = 0
   while i < n:
        if s[i] == s[j]:
            j += 1
            lps[i] = j
            i += 1
